{"timestamp":"2026-05-22T23:16:28.093Z","ordinal":3,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"# AGENTS.md instructions for /Users/zenray/Create/Build/Memory\n\n<INSTRUCTIONS>\n# Memory Repository — Codex Instructions\n\n## MemPalace MCP Integration\n\nThis project uses MemPalace for persistent semantic memory across sessions.\nPalace path: `D:/Create/Build/Memory/.mempalace`\n\n### On every session start\n1. Call `mempalace_status` to check palace health\n2. Call `mempalace_wake_up` (or read its output) for L0+L1 context\n\n### Before answering questions about past work, decisions, or history\n- Call `mempalace_search` with the relevant query\n\n### When learning something new and significant\n- Call `mempalace_add_drawer` with the content, wing=`memory`, appropriate room\n- Knowledge graph facts (who/what/when): call `mempalace_kg_add`\n\n### After a significant work session\n- Call `mempalace_diary_write` to log what happened\n\n## Existing file-based memory system\n\nThe markdown files in `memory/` are the **human-readable source of truth**.\nMemPalace is the **semantic search layer** on top — both systems coexist.\n\n- `memory/MEMORY.md` — master index (auto-loaded by Codex)\n- Individual `.md` files in `memory/` — detailed memory records\n\n## Rules\n- Never delete lines from memory markdown files (append-only)\n- Always read `Readme.md` before pushing\n- MemPalace data in `.mempalace/` is tracked in git for cloud backup\n\n## Clarté pédagogique — RÈGLE ABSOLUE\n\nToute chronologie, explication, synthèse, journal ou résumé doit être à la fois **limpide, synthétique, simple ET complexe** (ça ne s'oppose pas). Critère : un sales ET un développeur, un enfant de 8 ans, un homme de 40 ans, une mamie de 85 ans, doivent tous pouvoir comprendre le fond. Pas de jargon non expliqué, pas de bouillie technique, pas non plus de simplification mensongère. Si c'est complexe, le dire et le rendre lisible quand même